{"name":"Bonnie Dune Beach","hex":"#e4d1bc","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bonnie","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Merry; happy.","Beautiful; pretty; attractive; handsome."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bonfire; chiefly one several storeys tall and burned to celebrate Eleventh Night."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bonnie"},{"term":"dune","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A ridge or hill of sand piled up by currents of wind or water."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/dune"},{"term":"beach","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The shore of a body of water, especially when sandy or pebbly.","A horizontal strip of land, usually sandy, adjoining water."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To run aground on a beach.","To run (something) aground on a beach."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/beach"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bonnie","blocks":[{"text":"Bonnie is a Scottish feminine given name. It comes from the Scots language word \"bonnie\", or the French bonne (good). That is in turn derived from the Latin word \"bonus\" (good). The name can also be used as a pet form of Bonita."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d1/Rhett_and_Bonnie_Blue_Butler.jpg/330px-Rhett_and_Bonnie_Blue_Butler.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bonnie","wikidata":"Q4689423"},{"title":"Dune","blocks":[{"text":"A dune is a landform composed of wind- or water-driven sand. It typically takes the form of a mound, ridge, or hill. An area with dunes is called a dune system or a dune complex. A large dune complex is called a dune field, while broad, flat regions covered with wind-swept sand or dunes, with little or no vegetation, are called ergs or sand seas. Dunes occur in different shapes and sizes, but most kinds of dunes are longer on the stoss (upflow) side, where the sand is pushed up the dune, and have a shorter slip face in the lee side. The valley or trough between dunes is called a dune slack."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/61/Dunas_de_Maspalomas.jpg/330px-Dunas_de_Maspalomas.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dune","wikidata":"Q25391"},{"title":"Beach","blocks":[{"text":"A beach is a landform alongside a body of water which consists of loose particles. The particles composing a beach are typically made from rock, such as sand, gravel, shingle, pebbles, etc., or biological sources, such as mollusc shells or coralline algae. Sediments settle in different densities and structures, depending on the local wave action and weather, creating different textures, colors and gradients or layers of material."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg/330px-Beach_at_Fort_Lauderdale.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beach","wikidata":"Q40080"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Bonnie_and_Clyde_%281967_promo_photo_-_Dunaway%29.jpg/500px-Bonnie_and_Clyde_%281967_promo_photo_-_Dunaway%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/c6/Bonnie_and_Clyde_%281967_promo_photo_-_Dunaway%29.jpg/500px-Bonnie_and_Clyde_%281967_promo_photo_-_Dunaway%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Faye Dunaway as Bonnie Parker in the 1967 film Bonnie and Clyde.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABonnie_and_Clyde_(1967_promo_photo_-_Dunaway).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Saltation_on_sand_dune.png/330px-Saltation_on_sand_dune.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/56/Saltation_on_sand_dune.png/330px-Saltation_on_sand_dune.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Sand hitting sand is more likely to stick; sand hitting a more coherent surface is more likely to bounce (saltation). This exacerbating feedback loop helps sand accumulate into dunes.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ASaltation_on_sand_dune.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Barchan_in_Noachis.jpg/330px-Barchan_in_Noachis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Barchan_in_Noachis.jpg/330px-Barchan_in_Noachis.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Isolated barchan dunes on the surface of Mars. Dominant wind direction would be from left to right.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABarchan_in_Noachis.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Rub%27_al_Khali_%28Arabian_Empty_Quarter%29_sand_dunes_imaged_by_Terra_%28EOS_AM-1%29.jpg/250px-Rub%27_al_Khali_%28Arabian_Empty_Quarter%29_sand_dunes_imaged_by_Terra_%28EOS_AM-1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Rub%27_al_Khali_%28Arabian_Empty_Quarter%29_sand_dunes_imaged_by_Terra_%28EOS_AM-1%29.jpg/500px-Rub%27_al_Khali_%28Arabian_Empty_Quarter%29_sand_dunes_imaged_by_Terra_%28EOS_AM-1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/95/Rub%27_al_Khali_%28Arabian_Empty_Quarter%29_sand_dunes_imaged_by_Terra_%28EOS_AM-1%29.jpg/250px-Rub%27_al_Khali_%28Arabian_Empty_Quarter%29_sand_dunes_imaged_by_Terra_%28EOS_AM-1%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link"